0..76 Comment "// A loop drives an endpoint through a recursive protocol, one pass per turn"
77..96 Comment "// of the protocol."
97..99 Comment "//"
100..172 Comment "// A loop\'s passes are the passes of one fixpoint, and an endpoint bound"
173..249 Comment "// outside it would be captured by every pass. The loop threads the endpoint"
250..288 Comment "// instead, as it threads a held slot."
289..291 Comment "//"
292..371 Comment "// The lowering hands the endpoint to the loop\'s first pass and places it again"
372..449 Comment "// in each pass. The first pass takes it at the state the loop starts in, the"
450..528 Comment "// loop head\'s state, and `continue` hands it on at that state again. The loop"
529..562 Comment "// owes `Div` as every loop does."
563..565 Comment "//"
566..581 Comment "// - see: #4502"
582..662 Comment "// - see: #4705 — not implemented: a loop that acts on its endpoint every pass"
663..682 Comment "//   owing no `Div`"
683..745 Comment "// - see: #4687 — not implemented: running a placed endpoint"
747..821 Comment "/// A desk following a seat\'s reports until it retires: each report is one"
822..891 Comment "/// pass, and the retirement closes the endpoint and leaves the loop."
